PR #73's merge conflict resolution accidentally dropped the closing `}` for the `if (p === PipeShape.Chamber)` block in `_buildParamPanel()`, causing TypeScript to narrow `p` to `PipeShape.Chamber` for the rest of the function.

## Errors produced
- `TS2366`: `_buildParamPanel` missing return path (the `return panel` ended up inside the Chamber block)
- `TS2367` ×2: Unintentional comparisons — `p === PipeShape.Source` and `p === PipeShape.Sink` always false after narrowing
- `TS1128`: `private` keyword unexpected — `_buildGridSizePanel` parsed as a statement inside the unclosed block

## Fix

```ts
// Before (missing closing brace — `if (isChm)` incorrectly nested inside Chamber block)
if (p === PipeShape.Chamber) {
  ...
  panel.appendChild(selWrap);

if (isChm) {

// After
if (p === PipeShape.Chamber) {
  ...
  panel.appendChild(selWrap);
}

if (isChm) {
```

