`extension.ts` (desktop, 661 lines) and `web/extension.ts` (web, 437 lines) shared nearly identical activation logic, provider/command registration, event handlers, telemetry setup, and DI container composition.

## Changes

- **New `FabricVsCodeExtensionBase`** (`extension/src/FabricVsCodeExtensionBase.ts`): Base class containing all shared logic — `activate`, `registerViews`, `registerProviders`, `registerCommands`, `setupEventHandlers`, `initializeExtensionManager`, `setupTelemetry`, `deactivate`. Uses the Template Method pattern with protected hooks (`beforeActivate`, `afterActivate`) for platform-specific injection points. Also exports `composeBaseContainer()` with all common DI registrations.

- **Desktop `extension.ts`** (661 → 357 lines): `FabricVsCodeExtension extends FabricVsCodeExtensionBase`, overriding only desktop-specific concerns: local project view, export/local-project commands, URI handler, MCP server prompt, and test hooks. `composeContainer` delegates to `composeBaseContainer` and appends `LocalFolderManager`, `GitOperator`, `ExtensionUriHandler`, and mock/fake overrides.

- **Web `web/extension.ts`** (437 → 55 lines): `FabricVsCodeWebExtension extends FabricVsCodeExtensionBase` with no method overrides — all behavior inherited. `composeContainer` delegates to `composeBaseContainer` and appends `WebLocalFolderManager` and `WebGitOperator`.

```typescript
// Desktop adds platform-specific behavior via overrides
export class FabricVsCodeExtension extends FabricVsCodeExtensionBase {
    protected override async beforeActivate(): Promise<void> {
        void this.promptMcpServerInstall(); // non-blocking
    }
    protected override async registerViews(): Promise<vscode.TreeView<FabricTreeNode>> {
        const treeView = await super.registerViews();
        // ... register local project view
        return treeView;
    }
    // ...
}

// Web inherits everything — no overrides needed
export class FabricVsCodeWebExtension extends FabricVsCodeExtensionBase { }
```

