The chat window was broken on mobile because `position: absolute` on `.chat-window` resolved relative to the small `.chatbot-bubble` container rather than the viewport, making `width/height: 100%` expand to the bubble's size instead of the screen. Additionally, `bottom`/`right` adjustments in the mobile breakpoint were applied to `.chat-button` (no positioning context) instead of `.chatbot-bubble`.

## Changes

- **`.chat-window` on mobile**: Override to `position: fixed` with explicit `top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0` so the window covers the full viewport
- **`.chatbot-bubble` on mobile**: Add `bottom: 1.5rem; right: 1.5rem` here (the actual fixed-position container)
- **`.chat-button` on mobile**: Remove the ineffectual `bottom`/`right` properties

```css
@media (max-width: 640px) {
    .chatbot-bubble {
        bottom: 1.5rem;   /* was incorrectly on .chat-button */
        right: 1.5rem;
    }
    .chat-window {
        position: fixed;  /* was absolute, relative to bubble container */
        top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
        width: 100%; height: 100%;
        border-radius: 0;
    }
}
```

