Five `ReferenceError`/`TypeError` crashes visible in the extension Errors panel, breaking form execution, toggle, nav readback, and TTS playback.

## Missing variable/function declarations (`popup.js`)

All four were used but never declared — crashed on first call:

```js
const _injectedTabs = new Set();          // used in injectScripts(), readbackNav()
const _permCache    = new Map();          // used in checkPermission()
let   _guidedMicTimer = null;             // used in _scheduleGuidedMicReopen()
const _tTimers = {};
function tStart(label) { ... }
function tEnd(label)   { ... }
```

- **`resolveToolName`** — called at `executeAction()` line 361 before `checkPermission()`; added implementation that maps `field_id` → permission tool name (`fill_field` default, individual names for high-risk prefixes like `invoice`, `total`, `tax`).

## AudioContext autoplay policy violation (`vision_observer.js`)

`new AudioContext()` was called inside `playAudio()` which fires on incoming WebSocket messages — before any user gesture. Chrome blocks this.

**Fix:** gate `AudioContext` creation behind a `_userGestured` flag. Audio arriving before the first gesture is buffered in `_pendingAudio[]` and drained on the first `click`/`keydown`/`touchend`:

```js
function playAudio(url) {
  if (!_userGestured) { _pendingAudio.push(url); return; }
  _playAudioNow(url);
}
document.addEventListener("click", _onUserGesture, { capture: true, passive: true });
```

## `Cannot set properties of null` (`popup.js` / `popup.html`)

- `id="toggle-label"` was missing from `popup.html` → `document.getElementById` returned `null`; `.textContent =` threw.  
- Added the `<span id="toggle-label">` element to the header toggle group.  
- Added `?.` optional chaining and `if (el)` guards throughout `setVoiceState`, `clearOutput`, `showResult`, `showError`, and the toggle/mic/replay event bindings so any future missing element degrades silently instead of crashing.

